  "notes": "USAGE:\n- {草|くさ}むしりをする (to weed)\n- {草|くさ}むしりに{疲|つか}れる (to get tired from weeding)\n\nNUANCE:\nA common chore in Japanese households with gardens. Often considered tedious but necessary work, especially in summer when weeds grow quickly.\n\nRELATED:\n- {草|くさ}{取|と}り (weeding - alternative term)\n- {雑草|ざっそう} (weeds)\n- {除草|じょそう} (weeding - more formal)",
